     "answer": "C （细节题） There were no trees.",
     "evidence": "P1\nWhen Julius Morton moved to Nebraska City in 1854, he faced a problem shared by many settlers in the territory: It was a treeless plain. That meant no trees for building materials, or for fuel.\n当朱利叶斯·莫顿于1854年迁居内布拉斯加城时，他面临着该地区许多移民共有的一个问题：这是一片没有树的平原。这意味着没有树木可作建筑材料，也没有树木可作燃料。",
