     "stem": "What does NASA's 1989 paper claim houseplants can do?",
     "stemZh": "NASA 1989年的论文声称室内植物能做什么?\nA) 增加室内有毒污染物。\nB) 吸收有毒化学物质。\nC) 美化家居环境。\nD) 吸收周围湿气。",
     "answer": "B（细节题）Absorb poisonous chemicals.",
     "evidence": "P1\nSince NASA published a paper in 1989 claiming that houseplants can soak up pollution and toxic chemicals, businesses and homeowners have increasingly invested in greenery to help clean their air.\n自从 NASA 于 1989 年发表一篇论文，宣称室内植物能吸走污染和有毒化学物质以来，企业和房主便越来越多地投资绿植来帮助净化空气。",
     "signal": "claiming 后接论文主张。录音开头 claiming that houseplants can soak up pollution and toxic chemicals 中的 claiming 直接对应题干的 claim，是论文主张的落点，紧跟其后的内容就是答案句。",
     "sub": "soak up pollution and toxic chemicals↔Absorb poisonous chemicals.soak up=Absorb，toxic=poisonous",
     "exclude": "A)与原文相反Add to indoor toxic pollutants. 盗用了录音里的 toxic chemicals（有毒化学物）一词，却把『吸走』反说成『增加』，与论文主张正好相反。\n借用原文：houseplants can soak up pollution and toxic chemicals\nC)未提及Beautify the home environment. 是植物『好看』的生活常识，录音从头到尾只谈净化空气、从未提美化，属凭常识硬填。\nD)原词陷阱Soak up surrounding moisture. 借用了答案句 soak up 这个动词，却把吸收对象从『污染物』偷换成『水分（moisture）』，录音并未说植物吸潮。\n借用原文：houseplants can soak up pollution and toxic chemicals",
