     "stem": "What do we learn about previous studies of young children reading electronic books?",
     "stemZh": "关于幼儿阅读电子书的以往研究，我们了解到什么？\nA) 它们得出了相互矛盾的结论。\nB) 它们以小规模样本为基础。\nC) 它们得出了出乎意料的结果。\nD) 它们关注的是年龄更小的孩子。",
     "answer": "A（细节题）They came to conflicting conclusions.",
     "evidence": "P2\nIn fact, multiple studies have found that electronic books support story comprehension and vocabulary gains beyond what is provided by printed books. But there's also work suggesting that children sometimes invest less mental effort in learning from electronic books, and that parents talk less about content when sharing such books.\n事实上，多项研究发现，电子书在故事理解和词汇增长上的助益超过纸质书。但也有研究表明，孩子有时在电子书上投入的脑力反而更少，父母在一起读这类书时谈论内容也更少。",
